  "summary_en": "Bahrain's 2017 Cloud First Policy directs government entities to evaluate cloud services in all ICT procurement. It adopts NIST cloud definitions and sets out migration criteria, security, data classification, data sovereignty and roles for entities, iGA and ICTGC. It has no AI or robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Government agencies must evaluate cloud-based services in all ICT procurements.",
   "Adopts NIST definition of cloud computing and its service and deployment models.",
   "Entities must monitor cloud usage and report monthly to ICTGC.",
   "ICTGC oversees implementation, audits compliance and arbitrates disputes.",
   "Covers cloud security principles, data classification, backup and data sovereignty."
